6773	{"artifactId":"HLD-b6c90b3e0240d36c","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-b6c90b3e0240d36c-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-09-23T17:52:48.300Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"cl1","ref":"c1","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon IPC handler map registers only daemon.{status,shutdown,backup,compact,debug-status} — there is no existing daemon update/restart/respawn IPC method (the update+restart capability is genuinely net-new).","evidence":"read src/daemon/index.ts:922 resolves to `'daemon.status': async () => {`, confirming daemon.status is a registered handler in the map. The grep for daemon.{status,shutdown,backup,compact,debug-status,update,restart,respawn} returns hits only in docs/design HTML for status/shutdown — no source hit registers a daemon.update/restart/respawn handler, consistent with the premise that the update+restart IPC is net-new. Exhaustiveness of the 5-method set was verified against the handler map during DEF and is not contradicted here.","action":"No change. The premise holds: daemon.status is registered (index.ts:922) and no update/restart/respawn IPC exists, so sc1 is genuinely net-new.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl2","ref":"c2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon.status handler at src/daemon/index.ts:922 returns a DaemonStatus object; adding an installedCommit field is a purely additive change to that existing object.","evidence":"read src/daemon/index.ts:922 = `'daemon.status': async () => {` — the daemon.status handler exists at exactly the cited line, so adding an installedCommit field to its returned DaemonStatus object is an additive change to a real, located surface.","action":"No change. Citation resolves verbatim.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl3","ref":"c1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon process is managed by scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, which provides start/stop/restart/update subcommands.","evidence":"grep cmd_(start|stop|restart|update) hits scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:207 cmd_start, :232 cmd_stop, :238 cmd_restart (which calls cmd_stop then cmd_start), plus a cmd_update — the four subcommands the premise names are all present in daemon-ctl.sh.","action":"No change. daemon-ctl.sh provides start/stop/restart/update as cited.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl4","ref":"c3","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"scripts/daemon-ctl.sh update fetches origin, merges --ff-only, and compares current rev-parse HEAD vs the incoming origin/branch commit — the installed-vs-upstream commit comparison the plugin mirrors.","evidence":"scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:81 `git -C \"$DAEMON_ROOT\" fetch --quiet origin \"$branch\"`, :93 `current=$(git -C \"$DAEMON_ROOT\" rev-parse HEAD)`, :104 `git -C \"$DAEMON_ROOT\" merge --ff-only \"$incoming\"` — the fetch + ff-merge + HEAD-vs-incoming comparison the premise describes is present verbatim in daemon-ctl.sh's update path.","action":"No change. The reusable commit-comparison sequence exists as cited.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl5","ref":"c3","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/shared/paths.ts defines the ~/.insrc layout (pidFile, sockFile, daemon home) used to locate the daemon root and pidfile.","evidence":"read src/shared/paths.ts:18 = `pidFile: join(INSRC_DIR, 'daemon.pid'),` — confirms paths.ts defines the ~/.insrc layout including the daemon pidfile.","action":"No change. Citation resolves.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl6","ref":"c4","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The VS Code plugin's daemon controller exposes a LifecycleAction union including 'start'|'stop'|'restart'|'update'.","evidence":"read vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts:16 = `export type LifecycleAction = 'start' | 'stop' | 'restart' | 'update';` — the un